-- task 03 func_sum — helper module, the second translation unit.
-- A separate file so the call crosses a module boundary, the same reason the Fortran,
-- Tcl, Vala, Racket and Janet rows split this task. `global function` is required for
-- the helper to be visible outside its own module.
--
-- The `<noinline>` annotation is what actually keeps the call: Nelua concatenates every
-- required module into one C translation unit, so without it gcc at -O2 inlines the
-- helper and deletes the loop. Measured: 0.0000 s for the plain cross-file call against
-- 0.0227 s for this one at 1e8 calls. It is emitted as
-- `NELUA_NOINLINE` = `__attribute__((noinline))` on gcc. See 03_func_sum.nelua.

global function add_one(n: integer): integer <noinline>
  return n + 1
end
